00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Captain Hector Barbossa is a fictional character of the Pirates of the Caribbean franchise,
depicted by Geoffrey Rush and appearing in all five films in the series.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Barbossa debuted in The Curse of the Black Pearl (2003) as the captain of the Black
Pearl and a cursed undead skeleton, where he dies at the end of the film.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
However, the character is revealed to have been resurrected by Tia Dalma by the end
of Dead Man's Chest, and has since appeared in an anti-heroic role.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Captain Barbossa was also one of the nine Pirate Lords in At World's End (2007), a privateer in service to King George II and the British Navy while also seeking revenge against
Blackbeard in On Stranger Tides (2011), as well as a rich rogue and influential leader of a prosperous pirate empire and fleet in Dead Men Tell No Tales (2017).

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Throughout the series, Barbossa has been conceptualized as a "dark
trickster" and the evil counterpart of Captain Jack Sparrow.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
In The Curse of the Black Pearl, it was revealed he was once the first mate of Jack, before he
eventually betrayed him and led a mutiny to take the Black Pearl, becoming Jack's sworn enemy.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
However, since At World's End, he and Jack have let
go of their grudge and became allies.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Ever since his appearance, Barbossa has received a highly positive reception by critics, with
praise towards Rush's performance and his interesting rivalry and friendship with Jack.

